 snapping her  neck  this was an unexpected and shocking  moment but also somewhat  underwhelming way for a powerful fairy  like ms dowling to exit the show  if you're a fara fan though you can take  solace in the subtle hint you might have  missed in the scene that suggests the  former headmistress may still be alive  notice how pharah's eyes light up just  before rosalind attacks her suggesting  she may be drawing on her own magic to  protect herself  against a likely attack from her nemesis  pharah's dead body may simply be an  illusion she's cast to full rosalind  like many of the other illusions we've  seen fairies cast in the show  and if you're at all skeptical then just  remember that skye's father andreas was  brought back from the dead despite the  seemingly lethal blow that silver landed  on him  and let's not forget that handy healing  power that bloom has either  the casting of terra and musa has been  problematic given how it raised both  latin and  asian representation in the new series  making this show's main cast less  diverse than the original naughties  animation  there is however a tease to a potential  resolution for fans disappointed that  lack of flora in the series when tara  reveals some more details about her  family to musa i've got this cousin  called flora my mom's called rose the  flora name drop  hopefully means that the og winx club  nature fairy who was modeled on jennifer  lopez will be introduced in a future  season  another missing founding fairy from the  animated series is techne the fairy of  technology  however there's a clue in the first  season that might have revealed her or  somebody closely related to her  in the third episode when bloom is  studying some of the alfia yearbooks the  camera deliberately goes in close on one  of the pages  lingering on it for several seconds  interestingly one of the names on the  page  devon walla is described as a science  fair winner  it looks like this description refers to  this former alumna of alfia here  who also appears in the center of this  group photo and who bloom commented was  a farrah fawcett look alike when she saw  her in a school photo on one of the  walls  the show seems to be calling attention  to this character and the fact that she  was particularly skilled at science  could imply that this is techner or if  not tekna herself  and somebody related to her for example  her mother of course it's possible that  this is just a tease to a brand new  original character that will be  introduced later on but either way it  seems likely she will have some  significance in a future  storyline also mentioned on the page is  somebody called sparta west red and if  you have any theories about techno or  either of these two characters comment  below  when bloom meets rosalind for the first  time the show seems to imply that the  voices bloom has been hearing calling to  her have been rosalinds all along  hello however if you go back and listen  to the ghostly voices that bloom  originally heard calling to her they  sound quite different to roslyn's voice  these may actually be a hint and tease  to daphne who was a type of spirit  guardian and sister to bloom in winx  club  similar to the mysterious voice calling  to bloom in the new show  daphne's ghost also called to bloom and  winks club to come and find her  i'm all around you blue i'm within you  bloom  i'll show you whoa  daphne daphne was also once a guardian  of the dragon flame and so if she  appears in the show  she'll likely have a part to play in  helping bloom learn about that power  althea's resident bad girl beatrix may  be an air fairy  however her name is a reference to the  villainous trick sisters from winx club  who were witches  beatrix also says that she's from astor  del which was apparently a village of  blood witches  suggesting it's possible that beatrix  will actually turn out to be a witch in  the show  rather than a fairy and although beatrix  appears to combine  various attributes of the three og  tricks i see darcy and stormi it  wouldn't surprise me if she discovers  she has a couple of villainous sisters  or relations in a future season  and if you were ever in any doubt that  bad boy riven would end up  joining beatrix on the dark side the  infamous book on his desk is a dead  giveaway  the overall theme of the prince by  machiavelli that it's justifiable to act  in an immoral way in order to achieve  political goals  also points to some of the themes in the  first season such as rosalind lying  about evacuating astadel  so she could destroy the blood witches  living there as well as the burned ones  another little detail about riven you  might have missed comes in the final  episode when he meets rosalind for the  first time  notice how both his and dale's eyes  light up as she enters the room which  could suggest that they have some latent  magical abilities  or the way that roslyn's eyes glowed at  the same time could imply that she's  cast a spell on them to pull them over  to her side as she takes control over  the school  there's a hint that we could see some of  the more interesting powers aisha had in  the animated series in fate  for clues let's take a look at the scene  where pharah is explaining to aisha  about her water-based powers  a mass of water is persistent and  reliable a drop of water  is unpredictable vague amorphous can you  isolate it can you maintain  that which fights form farah's  description of water as amorphous  could be a reference to morphix the name  of aisha's power source in winx club and  a magical malleable substance which the  fairy can create by rearranging water  molecules  i'm not sure whether the fate  showrunners will go there but there are  some really cool things like aisha's  morphic surfboard which could be awesome  to see in live action  more by the way there's also a hint in  fate that aisha might be a princess like  she is in winx club when stella tells  bloom to ask aisha what it means to lose  a crown jewel now that might not mean  much to a first welder so feel free to  ask your suite mate how big of a  screw-up that is  almost as big as giving it to her in the  first place another change from winx  club is musa being a mind fairy rather  than a fairy of music  there are however a few references in  the new series to her musical background  in the animation  from the dj poster on the wall by her  bed to how she listens to music on her  headphones whenever she wants to drown  out reading other people's emotions  to the fact that she tells riven she was  once a dancer i wouldn't expect a mind  fairy to have such good moves  i used to be a dancer fashion was a huge  part of winx club and fans of that  aspect of the og  show would likely be disappointed with  the costuming on fate  there is perhaps a small nod to winx  club fashion however when bloom is  surprised at how often stellar changes  their clothes each day  so casual thing that you're changing for  people have seen me in this outfit  already  they'll expect something different  people expect you to wear  multiple outfits a day and there's  another neat little homage to the og  series when bloom reveals that she was  born in 2004  a reference to how winx club first  premiered on italian tv in that year  and in case you didn't know abigail  cohen who plays bloom also starred in  netflix's chilling adventures of sabrina  as one of the three weird sisters and if  you're a fan of that show  check out my video with all the best  easter eggs and things you missed in the  final season of sabrina  tap here to watch that or follow the  link in the video description  so what did you think of fate the winx  saga and how it changed from the  animated series  and do you have any theories on what  you'd like to see in season two  leave all your thoughts and comments  down below and if you enjoyed this then  a thumbs up is hugely appreciated  tap left for my next netflix video  including a 